    "text": "Certainly! Below is the implementation of the `flip_case` Python function:\n\n```python\n    \"\"\"Flip lowercase characters to uppercase and uppercase to lowercase.\n\n    >>> flip_case('Hello')\n    'hELLO'\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    \n    i = 0\n    for char in string:\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            result.append(char.upper())\n        else:\n            result.append(char.lower())\n        i += 1\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```\n\nYou can test the function by using the provided test example in the comments:\n\n```\nimport doct\ndoctest.testmod()\n```\n\nThis will run the provided test and display the result.",
